# In Vercel each variable is set for Production (the public site, built from
# main), for Preview (the test copies built from feature, which read the same
# database and the same Stripe sandbox), or for both. Most are both: a preview
# has to work like the site to be worth testing. The exceptions say why below.

# Supabase
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-key
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key

# Stripe
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_your-key
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_your-key
# The signing secret of the webhook endpoint (Stripe → Workbench → Webhooks).
# Replacing the endpoint, which is how its API version moves, replaces the
# secret (docs/DECISIONS.md, "Stripe's API version is set in three places").
# Stripe calls only the public address, so a preview holds it unused.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_your-key

# Resend
RESEND_API_KEY=re_your-key
# The From: address on every email. Must be on a domain verified in Resend.
# A name here is ignored: emails go out under the site's name from the admin,
# and replies go to the address she sets in Conținut site → Email-uri.
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@your-domain.ro

# PostHog (visitor statistics). The project's key; the project must be on
# PostHog's EU cloud, where lib/analytics.ts always sends. Statistics are sent
# only from the address in NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL, so a local build or a preview
# sends nothing whatever key it has.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_your-key
# A deliberate test from localhost or a preview: lifts the address rule for
# that build and logs every event in the browser's console. Never in
# Production. Use a key from a test project, not the live one.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_DEBUG=1

# Cloudflare Turnstile. In Vercel, Production and Preview each have an entry
# of their own, and Preview's is for the feature branch alone: a preview of
# any other branch has no key, so its forms refuse to send.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAA-your-site-key
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=0x4AAAA-your-secret-key

# E2E tests (Playwright)
TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL=playwright-admin@test.local
TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me


# Public origin, no trailing slash. In Vercel, Production only: it names the
# public site, and statistics are counted only on pages served from it
# (lib/analytics.ts). Canonical URLs, share images and the links in emails are
# built from it; a preview, without it, builds them from the production
# address Vercel provides (lib/site-config.ts).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-site.vercel.app

# The daily job (/api/cron/daily, scheduled in vercel.json). Vercel sends it as
# a Bearer token; a random string of at least 16 characters. Without it the
# job refuses to run. In Vercel, Production only: scheduled jobs run only on
# the production deployment, and a preview without the secret refuses the
# job, which matters because a preview reads the live database.
CRON_SECRET=

# Vercel only, for Production and Preview; not needed on this machine, where
# Node allows it already. Vercel's functions refuse require() of an ES module
# unless this is set, and the sanitizer's jsdom needs it: without it every
# page that renders stored HTML answers 500 (docs/DECISIONS.md,
# "isomorphic-dompurify needs a switch in Vercel").
# NODE_OPTIONS=--experimental-require-module
